COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[1,"§Al-Fatihah\ndeeds\nStart your supplication by praising and glorifying Allah, just as Al-Fatiha begins [Praise be to Allah], then ask Him what you want as Al-Fatiha concludes.\nSurat Al-Fatiha is the greatest Surah in the Holy Quran, and is the most recited Surah on daily basis. Read its interpretation and reflect upon the meanings of its verses.\nIdentify a group of good and pious individuals and keep their company.\nguid\nThis Surah is divided between Allah and His servant. This portion: (You alone we worship), and what preceded it is for Allah; and this portion: (You alone we ask for help), and what followed is for the servant. Hence, reflect on .\nYou will not be able to worship Allah as He should be worshiped without His Help.\nBeware of following the approach of the Jews, (who put their desires before the commands of Allah), [Not those upon whom is the anger], or the approach of Christians, (who worship with innovation and ignorance).\nrefl\nٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ ٣ مَٰلِكِ يَوۡمِ ٱلدِّينِ ٤\nThis is as if Allah is saying: O My servants, if you praise and glorify the perfection of essence and attributes, then glorify Me, for I am \"Allah\"; if your praise is for benevolence and bounty, indeed I am \"The Lord of the worlds\"; if your praise is in hope for what is coming, indeed I am \"The Most Gracious, the Ever Merciful\", and if your praise is due to your fear, indeed I am \"The Master of the Day of Judgment.\" Al-Alusi: 1/86.\nWhat implications do the four attributes in this Surah have on praising Allah?\nبِسۡمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ ١ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ ٣ مَٰلِكِ يَوۡمِ ٱلدِّينِ ٤ إِيَّاكَ نَعۡبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسۡتَعِينُ ٥ ٱهۡدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلۡمُسۡتَقِيمَ ٦\nSince asking Allah for guidance to the Straight Path is a revered request and its attainment is the noblest gift from Allah, He taught His servants how to ask for it. He ordained that they praise and glorify Him before asking. Then, He mentions their servitude and their belief in His Oneness (Tawhīd), for these are two means to attain their goal. Therefore, seek the means to Him by His names and attributes and through your servitude to Him. No supplication which is accompanied by these two means will go unanswered. Ibn Al-Qayim: 1/36.\nIn these verses, two means for answering supplication are mentioned. What are they?\nإِيَّاكَ نَعۡبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسۡتَعِينُ ٥\nSeeking Allah's help is mentioned after worship, even though it is a part of it, because the servant needs Allah's help in performing all acts of worship; if Allah does not help him, he will not attain what he aspires of fulfilling commands and avoiding prohibitions.Al-Saadi: 39.\nSeeking Allah's help is mentioned after worship, even though it is a part of it. Why?\nإِيَّاكَ نَعۡبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسۡتَعِينُ ٥\nWorship is the highest level of submissiveness, and it is not permissible, according to Sharia and reason, to do it except for Allah, because He is alone worthy of it, as He is the Giver of the greatest blessings of life, existence, and everything they entail. Al-Alusi: 1/86.\nWhy is worship must be directed to Allah alone?\nإِيَّاكَ نَعۡبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسۡتَعِينُ ٥ ٱهۡدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلۡمُسۡتَقِيمَ ٦\nThe use of the pronoun (we) for worship signifies that prayer is a collective activity. Al-Biqai: 1/17.\nIn this Surah, why is the plural form used with these words: Worship, reliance and supplication?\nٱهۡدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلۡمُسۡتَقِيمَ ٦\nThe need for guidance is more important than the need for victory or sustenance. In fact, there is no comparison between the two because once the servant is guided he becomes righteous, (and whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out and will provide for him from where he does not expect). Ibn Taimyah: 1/116.\nThe need for guidance is more important than the need for victory or sustenance. Why?\nٱهۡدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلۡمُسۡتَقِيمَ ٦\nSteadiness of the servant on the bridge that Allah set up over Hellfire on the Last Day depends on his steadiness on the path of Allah in this life, and he will cross that bridge then in the same manner that he conducts his life here. Some will cross as fast as lightning, and some will cross in a blink of an eye. Therefore, one should reflect on crossing that bridge on the Last Day in comparison to how well he follows the path of Allah in this life, a befitting recompense for his deeds, (Are you recompensed except for what you used to do) [27-90]. Ibn Al-Qayim: 1/35.\nWhat is the link between following the path of Allah in this life and crossing of the bridge over Hellfire on the Last Day?\nwords\nبِسْمِ اللَّهِI begin my recital with the help of Allah\nيوم الدينThe Day of Recompense\nغير المغضوبJews and the likes of them who do not practice what they know to be the truth\nالضالينChristians and the likes of them who act without knowledge"],[2,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nRighteousness is based on the fact that Allah's Sharia often goes against your desires so as to test your faith. Identify something in your life that you feel you are putting your own desires before Allah's Sharia, and turn away from it, seeking forgiveness from your Lord.\nReckon with yourself concerning your prayer, examine today the aspects of shortcomings and complete them in the manner required by the Sharia.\nTest your certain faith in the Last Day by spending today out of Allah's wealth, given to you by Him, while you are certain that He will compensate you for it in this life and the Hereafter.\nguid\nRighteousness (fearing Allah) is a path for attaining guidance through the Quran, hence, always put Allah's Sharia ahead of your desires.\nYour happiness lies in success that can only be attained by those who have these qualities:\nThe most important traits of the believers is their steadfastness in faith in the witnessed and the unseen, and being mindful of Allah at all times.\nrefl\nالٓمٓ ١ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبُ لَا رَيۡبَۛ فِيهِۛ هُدٗى لِّلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٢\nThese separated letters were stated at the beginning of some Surahs to assert the inimitability of the Quran, and the fact that mankind is incapable of matching its eloquent level even though it is made up of these letters by which they speak. Therefore; each Surah that begins with these letters mentions the supremacy, inimitability, and greatness of the Quran, and this is known by induction. Ibn Kathir: 1/36-37.\nWhat is the link between the separated letters and induction of greatness and inimitability of the Quran?\nذَٰلِكَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبُ لَا رَيۡبَۛ فِيهِۛ هُدٗى لِّلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٢\nAllah does not say guidance for a specific interest or thing. Rather, it is left generalized because the Quran is a general guidance to all benefits of this life and the Hereafter. The Quran is a guidance for servants in all issues, both fundamental and incidental; it clearly separates truth from falsehood, sound from weak, and shows them how to follow the paths that are beneficial to them in this life and the Hereafter. Al-Saadi: 40.\nHow it can be inferred from this verse that guidance of the Quran is inclusive of all benefits of both this life and the Hereafter?\nٱلَّذِينَ يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱلۡغَيۡبِ وَيُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ يُنفِقُونَ ٣\nBelieving in the unseen is a role of the heart, establishing prayer is a role of the body,(and spend out of what We have provided for them) is a role of wealth, which is all apparent. Al-Qurtubi: 1/274.\nThis verse combines three aspects of righteousness, what are they?\nوَيُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ\nAllah does not say that they \"do\" or \"perform\" the prayer, because it is not sufficient to merely perform its outward form. Establishing prayer means establishing its outward form completely, fulfilling its pillars, obligations, and conditions, as well as establishing it inwardly by performing its essence, which is attentiveness of the heart, and reflecting on what one says and acts in it. Al-Saadi: 41.\nThe word (Establish) is used for performing prayer. Why?\nوَمِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ يُنفِقُونَ\n(Out of) is used to indicates \"some\" in order to signal to them that only a fraction of their wealth is required for spending, which would not cause them any harm or overburden. In fact, they would gain a reward, and their needy brethren would benefit. (Of what We have provided for them) is an indication that the wealth in your possession is not gained by your own power, but rather it is the provision of Allah that He has bestowed upon you. Just as Allah has favored you over many of His servants [by giving you this wealth], thank Him by giving out some of what He has bestowed upon you. Al-Saadi: 41.\nWhat is the significance of using (out of)?\nٱلَّذِينَ يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱلۡغَيۡبِ وَيُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ يُنفِقُونَ ٣\nBelieving in the unseen entails spending because provision from Allah is, in fact, part of the unseen, and therefore; when the servant is certain of receiving compensation from Allah for his spending, he will spend even more; and when he extends his favors to others, his succession on earth will be fulfilled, his authority will be expanded, and more bountiful provision will come his way. Al-Biqai: 1/30.\nWhy does spending depend on believing in the unseen?\nوَبِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ هُمۡ يُوقِنُونَ\nCertainty is the highest level of knowledge with which there is no doubt. Ibn Atiyah: 1/86.\nThe more certainty in believing in the Hereafter, the more deeds are exerted for it, explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nالمThe Quran is made up of these letters, yet no one is capable of matching it\nلِلمُتَّقِينَThose who shield themselves from the punishment of Allah by doing good and avoiding evil"],[3,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nExplain to those around you the risk and lies of those who claim that they defend women's rights while, in fact; their aim is to exploit them.\nSeek refuge with Allah from hypocrisy.\nPray today that Allah protects the Muslim nation from the evil of the hypocrites.\nguid\nDisobedience may be a reason for Allah to put a seal upon the heart so that it cannot reach the truth.\nAllah identifies the state of the disbelievers in two verses, then details the description of hypocrites in thirteen verses because they are more dangerous than the disbelievers, as the hypocrites deceive the common Muslims.\nDespising and belittling the righteous are some of the characteristics of hypocrites.\nrefl\nخَتَمَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ وَعَلَىٰ سَمۡعِهِمۡۖ\nWhen sins swarm the hearts successively, the hearts become locked which caused it to be sealed and stamped by Allah. Hence, faith will have no way to them, and disbelief will have no escape from them. This is the seal and stamp mentioned in the Almighty's saying: (Allah has set a seal upon their hearts and upon their hearing). Ibn Kathir: 1/45.\nHow does the heart become sealed?\nخَتَمَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ وَعَلَىٰ سَمۡعِهِمۡۖ وَعَلَىٰٓ أَبۡصَٰرِهِمۡ غِشَٰوَةٞۖ\nAllah mentions the obstacles that prevented them from believing, saying: (Allah has set a seal upon their hearts); He set an impenetrable seal through which faith cannot enter, and so they do not comprehend what benefits them nor can they hear what is useful to them. (And over their sight is a veil); a cover blocks their sights from seeing what benefits them. The heart, hearing and sight are paths for knowledge and goodness; when they are blocked, no good is expected from them. They were prevented from goodness and the gates of faith were closed to them because of their disbelief and denial. Al-Saadi: 42.\nWhy were these senses, (heart, hearing, and sight) selected to be sealed and covered?\nخَتَمَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ وَعَلَىٰ سَمۡعِهِمۡۖ وَعَلَىٰٓ أَبۡصَٰرِهِمۡ غِشَٰوَةٞۖ وَلَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٞ ٧\nThe mention of hearing before sight in the Quran is an indication of the fact that hearing is more beneficial to the person since precedence denotes importance, as hearing is the instrument for receiving knowledge through which the mind is perfected. It is the means of conveying the message of the Prophets to their nations in a more complete manner than conveying it through sight alone. Ibn Ashour: 1/258.\nAudio means versus visual means: Which has more impact on people?\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَقُولُ ءَامَنَّا بِٱللَّهِ وَبِٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ وَمَا هُم بِمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٨\nAfter describing the believers in the beginning of the Surah in four verses, then defining the state of the disbelievers in these two verses, Allah describes the state of the hypocrites who show faith but conceal disbelief, since their situation is confusing to many people, He elaborated on mentioning them with various characteristics. Ibn Kathir: 1/45.\nAllah describes the believers in four verses, and the disbelievers in two verses, but He describes the hypocrites in thirteen verses. Why?\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَقُولُ ءَامَنَّا بِٱللَّهِ وَبِٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ وَمَا هُم بِمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٨\nAllah warns of the characteristics of hypocrites so that the believers will not be deceived by their outward appearance, thus widespread corruption will occur due to not being cautious of them and believing that they are believers while, in reality, they are not. This is considered a major prohibition. Ibn Kathir: 1/46.\nWhy is it important for the believers to recognize the state of hypocrites?\nفِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ فَزَادَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ مَرَضٗاۖ وَلَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمُۢ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَكۡذِبُونَ ١٠\n(In their hearts is a sickness), that is because of their content with this world and their love for it, and are heedless of the Hereafter and turn away from it. (Allah has increased their sickness), which means that He forsake them and loaded them with the worries of this world, so that they could not devote themselves the religion. (And they will have a painful punishment) caused by what perishes that deprives them of the lasting good. Al-Junaid said: \"Sickness of the heart comes from following desires, just as the illnesses of the limbs come from illness of the body.\" Al-Qurtubi: 1/300.\nWhat causes the sickness in the hearts of hypocrites?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱشۡتَرَوُاْ ٱلضَّلَٰلَةَ بِٱلۡهُدَىٰ فَمَا رَبِحَت تِّجَٰرَتُهُمۡ وَمَا كَانُواْ مُهۡتَدِينَ ١٦\nThey preferred misguidance, like a buyer who wants a particular item so much so that he is willing to pay a very high price. This is one of the best examples, where it depicts misguidance, which is the ultimate evil, as a commodity, and depicts guidance, which is the ultimate goodness, as the price. Al-Saadi: 43.\nHow can misguidance be purchased for guidance?\nwords\nخَتَمَ اللَّهُAllah has set a seal\nغِشَاوَةٌVeil\nمَرَضٌDoubt and hypocrisy\nيَعمَهُونَThey bewilder and are oblivious to guidance"],[4,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nRead an example from the Quran, today, and try to understand it.\nThe light in the heart is from Allah, so ask Allah by saying, \"Let there be light in my heart, in my hearing and in my sight.\"\nReflect on this verse, then draw a useful lesson and share it in a message.\nguid\nWorshiping Allah, the Almighty, is the purpose of your existence.\nReflection on the creations of Allah increases certainty and faith in the heart of the servant.\nAssociating partners with Allah Who has honored you is a sign of a defective logic and an invalid belief.\nrefl\nمَثَلُهُمۡ كَمَثَلِ ٱلَّذِي ٱسۡتَوۡقَدَ نَارٗا فَلَمَّآ أَضَآءَتۡ مَا حَوۡلَهُۥ ذَهَبَ ٱللَّهُ بِنُورِهِمۡ وَتَرَكَهُمۡ فِي ظُلُمَٰتٖ لَّا يُبۡصِرُونَ ١٧\nIf it is said: What is the reason for likening the hypocrites to the owner of the fire that was lit up and then darkened? The answer is threefold, first: Their worldly gain in this life by claiming faith resembles light, and their punishment in the Hereafter resembles darkness. Second: Hiding their disbelief resembles the light, and their disgrace afterward resembles darkness. Third: This relates to those among them who accepted faith which resembles light, and their denial and disbelief afterward resembles darkness; this explanation is supported by another verse, (that is because they believed, then disbelieved) [63:3].Ibn Juzay: 1/54.\nWhat is the reason for likening the hypocrites to the owner of the fire that was lit up and then darkened?\nصُمُّۢ بُكۡمٌ عُمۡيٞ فَهُمۡ لَا يَرۡجِعُونَ ١٨\nAllah says about them: (Deaf), unable to hear the truth. (Dumb), unable to speak the truth. (Blind), unable to see the truth. (So they will not return [to the straight path]), because they have forsaken the truth after having come to know it, so they will not return to it, unlike those who kept away from the truth as the result of ignorance and misguidance because they did not understand it, however, they are more likely to come back to the truth than the hypocrites would. Al-Saadi: 44.\nAllah describes the hypocrites saying: (So they will not return). Why?\nوَلَوۡ شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ لَذَهَبَ بِسَمۡعِهِمۡ وَأَبۡصَٰرِهِمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٞ ٢٠\nIn this verse, Allah describes Himself as having the power to do all things, because He warns the hypocrites of His punishment and power, and informs them that He is completely encompasses them, and is able to take away their hearing and sight.Ibn Kathir: 1/55.\nThis verse concludes with describing Allah as the Most Capable of all things. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ ٱعۡبُدُواْ رَبَّكُمُ ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَكُمۡ وَٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۡ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَتَّقُونَ ٢١\n(Worship your Lord): This includes faith in Allah, the belief in His Oneness (Tawhīd), and obedience to Him. Allah commands faith of the disbeliever, Tawhīd of the polytheist, and obedience of the believer. Ibn Juzay: 1/56.\nList the types of people who are commanded by this verse.\nفَلَا تَجۡعَلُواْ لِلَّهِ أَندَادٗا وَأَنتُمۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ ٢٢\nThis verse is a clear and precise command upon which all revealed religions and divine Books have agreed. It is the pillar of humility and the essence of humbleness and submissiveness to Allah. Al-Biqai: 1/59.\nThis verse contains a rule for worshiping Allah. What is it?\nوَإِن كُنتُمۡ فِي رَيۡبٖ مِّمَّا نَزَّلۡنَا عَلَىٰ عَبۡدِنَا فَأۡتُواْ بِسُورَةٖ مِّن مِّثۡلِهِۦ وَٱدۡعُواْ شُهَدَآءَكُم مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ إِن كُنتُمۡ صَٰدِقِينَ ٢٣ فَإِن لَّمۡ تَفۡعَلُواْ وَلَن تَفۡعَلُواْ\nMeaning: They will never be able to answer the challenge. This is another miracle, in that, Allah clearly and decisively states, without fear or concern, that the Quran will never be opposed or challenged by anything similar to it for eternity. And so it happened, it has not been opposed from its time until our time, and it is not possible, and how could that be possible for anyone? Ibn Kathir: 1/58.\nThis verse indicates a clear miracle for the Holy Quran. Explain.\nوَقُودُهَا ٱلنَّاسُ وَٱلۡحِجَارَةُۖ أُعِدَّتۡ لِلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٢٤\nAllah mentions people first as a fuel for Hellfire because they are the ones who perceive pain, or because they are more flammable than inanimate objects due to their skin, meat, and fat. It is also more frightening to think of people as being a fuel for Hellfire. Al-Alusi: 1/199.\nAllah mentions people before stones as a fuel for Hellfire. Why?\nwords\nبُكمٌUnable to speak the truth\nكَصَيِّبٍHeavy rain\nأَندَادًاCounterpart, parallel\nرَيبٍDoubt"],[5,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nFrom among the rewards in Paradise mentioned in the Quran, write down three that you wish for.\nRecall a promise that you made but did not fulfill, and hasten to fulfill it at once.\nVisit some of your relatives today, send a gift or call and ask about them.\nguid\nHaving a residence, a provision, a wife, and protection from death are all wishes of mankind, but they can only be attained and become permanent in Paradise.\nWhen a believer receives a command from Allah, he accepts it with submission and compliance. As for the hypocrite, he argues much with the intention of invalidating it.\nFaith earns the believer an insight by which he can distinguish truth from falsehood.\nrefl\nوَبَشِّرِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\nIt is encouraged to give glad tidings to the believers and motivate them to do good deeds by mentioning the rewards and incentives, as this will make doing such deeds light and easy. Al-Saadi: 47.\nWhat is the importance of receiving glad tidings in the lives of the believers?\nوَبَشِّرِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ أَنَّ لَهُمۡ جَنَّٰتٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُۖ\nMu'ath bin Jabal (t) said: \"A righteous deed consists of four things: Knowledge, intention, patience and sincerity.\" Al-Baghawi 1/27.\nWhen is a deed considered righteous?\nوَبَشِّرِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ أَنَّ لَهُمۡ جَنَّٰتٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُۖ\nThe beauty of the gardens is complemented by the water flowing through them, which is something that all humans agree is one of the most beautiful sights. Ibn Ashur: 1/354.\nThis verse states that the rivers flow underneath the gardens. Why?\nوَلَهُمۡ فِيهَآ أَزۡوَٰجٞ مُّطَهَّرَةٞۖ\nWhen describing them as purified, Allah does not specify a certain defect, which indicates that they will be pure in all aspects. They will be pure in terms of their manner and character, free of physical defects, pure in speech and chaste in their gaze. Al-Saadi: 46.\nAllah describes the women in Paradise as (purified) in general. Why?\nوَهُمۡ فِيهَا خَٰلِدُونَ\nThis is the ultimate happiness, for the believers will enjoy everlasting delight, safe from death and disruption of their bliss, and it will never end or cease. Ibn Kathir: 1/61.\nWhy is the mention of the bliss of the people of Paradise concluded with them being eternal in it?\nوَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ فَيَقُولُونَ مَاذَآ أَرَادَ ٱللَّهُ بِهَٰذَا مَثَلٗاۘ يُضِلُّ بِهِۦ كَثِيرٗا وَيَهۡدِي بِهِۦ كَثِيرٗاۚ وَمَا يُضِلُّ بِهِۦٓ إِلَّا ٱلۡفَٰسِقِينَ ٢٦\nThis is a rebuke to anyone who is misguided by misinterpreting the Quran, he is \"Fasiq\" (defiantly disobedient), not because he was \"Fasiq\" before that. Saad bin Abi Waqqas (t) inferred from this verse that Al-Khawarij (a deviant sect) were defiantly disobedient since they were misguided by misinterpreting the Quran. Hence, whoever is misguided by misinterpreting the Quran is Fasiq. Ibn Taimyah: 1/187.\nWhoever distorts the meanings of the Holy Quran far from the way of the righteous predecessors is \"Fasiq\". Explain.\nيُضِلُّ بِهِۦ كَثِيرٗا وَيَهۡدِي بِهِۦ كَثِيرٗاۚ وَمَا يُضِلُّ بِهِۦٓ إِلَّا ٱلۡفَٰسِقِينَ ٢٦\nThat is: By the blessing of their belief in goodness and their submission to their Lord, He guides them through their faith, makes them understand what is intended by it, and opens their hearts to the knowledge it contains, thus increasing their faith, reassurance and certainty. In reality, the guided are many, but they are few in comparison to the misguided. Al-Biqai: 1/77.\nWho is more likely to receive Allah's guidance for understanding the Quran?\nwords\nمُتَشَابِهًاResembles one another in color and form but not in taste\nاستَوَىHe turned toward"],[6,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nMake a schedule for yourself to learn the most important issues you need.\nRead the story of Adam (u) from books of Quran interpretation and Prophets stories, then draw three lessons that are important for your life.\nRecall a sin committed by you or your immediate family and say:\nguid\nKnow the value of scholars and be polite with them, as Allah Has commanded the angels to prostrate before Adam because of his knowledge.\nGlorifying Allah is one of the attributes of angels, so be like them.\nBe humble to Allah, no matter how knowledgeable you think you are, and ask Him to increase your knowledge.\nrefl\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ إِنِّي جَاعِلٞ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ خَلِيفَةٗۖ\nThis verse is a sound evidence for appointing an Imam or a Caliph (a Ruler) who is obeyed so he can unite the people and implement the laws. This obligatory duty (appointing a Ruler) is agreed upon unanimously among the scholars and the Muslim nation. Al-Qurtubi: 1/395.\nFor the Muslim nation to be without a Ruler is considered a grave sin due to the resulting chaos and corruptions. Explain.\nأَتَجۡعَلُ فِيهَا مَن يُفۡسِدُ فِيهَا وَيَسۡفِكُ ٱلدِّمَآءَ\nThese two reasons, causing corruption and shedding blood, mentioned by the angels, are the same two reasons for which Allah ordained legal retribution for the Children of Israel. Ibn Taimyah 1/192.\nWhat are the two reasons that if spread will lead to the destruction of nations?\nأَتَجۡعَلُ فِيهَا مَن يُفۡسِدُ فِيهَا وَيَسۡفِكُ ٱلدِّمَآءَ وَنَحۡنُ نُسَبِّحُ بِحَمۡدِكَ وَنُقَدِّسُ لَكَۖ\nThe angels' statement was not an objection to Allah, nor was it an envy of the Children of Adam, but rather it was a question of inquiry of the wisdom behind that. Ibn Kathir: 1/67.\nAllah censured Iblis for his question but did not blame the angels for their question. Why?\nقَالُوٓاْ أَتَجۡعَلُ فِيهَا مَن يُفۡسِدُ فِيهَا وَيَسۡفِكُ ٱلدِّمَآءَ\n(Will You place upon it one who causes corruption therein) by committing sin, (and sheds blood) although this is included in the meaning of the previous general statement (causes corruption); nevertheless, it is mentioned here in order to highlight the seriousness of killing. Al-Saadi: 48.\nWhy is shedding blood specified even though it is included in causing corruption?\nقَالُواْ سُبۡحَٰنَكَ لَا عِلۡمَ لَنَآ إِلَّا مَا عَلَّمۡتَنَآۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ٣٢\nIt is obligatory for someone who is asked about something he does not know to say: \"Allah knows best, I do not know,\" following the example of the angels, Prophets, and virtuous scholars. The Prophet (r) stated that with the death of scholars, knowledge will be taken away, leaving ignorant people who will be asked for \"fatwas\" and they will issue \"fatwas\" according to their own opinions, so they will go astray and lead others astray. Al-Qurtubi: 1/425.\nWhat do we learn from the angels saying: \"Glory be to You! We have no knowledge except what You have taught us\"?\nوَلَا تَقۡرَبَا هَٰذِهِ ٱلشَّجَرَةَ فَتَكُونَا مِنَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٣٥\nThe prohibition against approaching the tree implies the prohibition against eating from it in the first instance. Forbidding the approach is an example of a principle in Fiqh called: \"Blocking the means.\" Ibn Juzay: 1/62.\nWhat is the best way to avoid committing sins?\nفَتَلَقَّىٰٓ ءَادَمُ مِن رَّبِّهِۦ كَلِمَٰتٖ فَتَابَ عَلَيۡهِۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلتَّوَّابُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٣٧\nAllah's mercy precedes His punishment; He shows His mercy toward His servant in the midst of His wrath, just as He made the descending of Adam to earth a reason for his ascension, and Adam's remoteness a cause for his closeness to Him. Glory be to Him, the Forgiver, how honorable He is, and the Merciful, how great He is. Al-Alusi: 1/238.\nAfter reading the story of Adam (u), we should not despair of Allah's mercy. Explain.\nwords\nوَيَسفِكُSheds blood\nنقدس لکWe declare Your perfection\nرَغَدًاEat therefrom in ease and abundance\nفَأَزَلَّهُمَاHe caused them to slip into sin"],[7,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nRemind those around you, today, of Allah's favors which He bestowed upon you all, and the need to be grateful to Him for them so they would last.\nToday, be sure to arrive early for congregational prayer, remind others of its virtue, and glorify Allah much when bowing.\nIdentify a wrong action that you struggle to quit and warn others about it. Perhaps this will make you feel modest before Allah and give it up for good.\nguid\nFollowing Islamic teachings brings security and reassurance of the heart. It removes fear and distress in this life and the Hereafter.\nDo not make your objective of memorizing and understanding the Book of Allah (Holy Quran) to gain the pleasures of this worldly life.\nLife, indeed, becomes easier with patience and prayer.\nrefl\nيَٰبَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ\nAllah commands the Jews to embrace Islam and follow Muhammad (r). He provokes them by mentioning the example of their father Israel, Allah's Prophet Jacob (u), as if saying, \"O children of the righteous and obedient servant of Allah, be like your father in following the truth.\" This is similar to one's saying, \"O son of that generous man, do this or that,\" or \"O son of the brave man, engage the strong fighters,\" or \"O son of the scholar, seek knowledge,\" and so on. Ibn Kathir: 1/79.\nAllah calls the Jews as the descendants of their father Jacob (u). Why?\nوَءَامِنُواْ بِمَآ أَنزَلۡتُ مُصَدِّقٗا لِّمَا مَعَكُمۡ وَلَا تَكُونُوٓاْ أَوَّلَ كَافِرِۢ بِهِۦۖ\nThe Quran's confirmation of the Torah and other revelations, and Prophet Muhammad's (r) confirmation of the Prophets before him has three aspects: First: The Prophets before Muhammad (r) revealed that he would come, and then he did as they said, thus proving their truthfulness. Second: He confirmed their Prophethood and their revealed Scriptures, hence, he attested to their truthfulness. Third: The Quran and Muhammad's (r) teachings are in agreement with what is in their Scriptures regarding the Oneness of Allah (Tawhīd), mention of the Hereafter, and religious beliefs, thus, he confirmed them since they all share the same faith in these beliefs. Ibn Juzay: 1/64.\nHow does the Quran confirm previous Scriptures?\nوَلَا تَشۡتَرُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِي ثَمَنٗا قَلِيلٗا وَإِيَّٰيَ فَٱتَّقُونِ ٤١\nAlthough this verse addresses the Children of Israel, it applies to anyone who does what they did. Whoever takes a bribe to change or invalidate a right, or refrains from teaching what is required of him, or from performing what he has learned—which is required of him—in order to receive a reward, then he falls within the meaning of this verse. Al-Qurtubi: 2/11.\nWhen can one be described as trading Allah's verses for a small price?\nوَلَا تَلۡبِسُواْ ٱلۡحَقَّ بِٱلۡبَٰطِلِ وَتَكۡتُمُواْ ٱلۡحَقَّ وَأَنتُمۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ ٤٢\nThe verse is used as evidence that one who knows the truth must reveal it, and it is forbidden for him to conceal it, in accordance with the conditions known to scholars. Al-Alusi: 1/247.\nWhat is inferred from this verse?\nأَتَأۡمُرُونَ ٱلنَّاسَ بِٱلۡبِرِّ وَتَنسَوۡنَ أَنفُسَكُمۡ\nThe intent is not to censure them for enjoining righteousness while abandoning doing it, but rather for abandoning enjoining righteousness. Enjoining good is a part of righteousness and is an obligation for scholars; who themselves are required to heed, and adhere to that which they preach others. Enjoining righteousness and performing righteousness are both required. Neither one is rendered unnecessary when omitting the other. Ibn Kathir: 1/82.\nWhen a sinner sees another person committing the same sin, should he remain silent about it?\nوَٱسۡتَعِينُواْ بِٱلصَّبۡرِ وَٱلصَّلَوٰةِۚ وَإِنَّهَا لَكَبِيرَةٌ إِلَّا عَلَى ٱلۡخَٰشِعِينَ ٤٥\nAllah, the Almighty, says that establishing prayer is difficult for everyone except those who have the above-mentioned trait. Al-Tabari: 1/22.\nWhat is the trait that endears prayer to the believer and makes him long for it?\nوَٱسۡتَعِينُواْ بِٱلصَّبۡرِ وَٱلصَّلَوٰةِۚ وَإِنَّهَا لَكَبِيرَةٌ إِلَّا عَلَى ٱلۡخَٰشِعِينَ ٤٥\nPrayer is not burdensome for the humbly submissive because they value its positive effects on them, and anticipate the reward stored up for them, so it is easy for them. It is said that whoever knows the value of what he seeks, giving will be easy for him, and whoever is certain of the return, will be generous with his gift. Al-Alusi: 1/249.\nPrayer is not difficult for the humbly submissive to Allah. Why?\nwords\nفَارهَبُونِFear none but Me\nوَلاَ تَلبِسُواDo not mix\nيَظُنُّونَThey are sure\nعَدلٌRansom"],[8,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nPrepare a list of calamities and dangers from which Allah have saved the society, and share it along with a reminder to thank Allah Who likes those who are grateful to Him at all times.\nRemind a heedless person that the condition for repentance of the sinners of Children of Israel was that they kill themselves, but as for the sinners of the nation of Prophet Muhammad (r), Allah made it easier for them by limiting them to seeking forgiveness with sincere repentance.\nReview the food items that you consume and keep off items that are prohibited or have doubtful sources. Good and \"Halal\" substitutes are in abundance so limit yourself to eating the good things.\nguid\nThe greater the injustice of a tyrant, the sooner his reign will come to an end.\nDo not despair because of your many sins. If Allah forgives polytheism (shirk) -which is the greatest of sins- when the servant repents from it, then all you have to do is turn to Allah with sincere repentance.\nIt is from Allah's mercy to His servants that He gives them respite and does not hasten to punish them, so that they may repent to Him and seek His forgiveness, and so He forgives them.\nrefl\nوَأَغۡرَقۡنَآ ءَالَ فِرۡعَوۡنَ وَأَنتُمۡ تَنظُرُونَ ٥٠\nWe drowned them while you were watching in order to heal your hearts and humiliate your enemy. Ibn Kathir: 1/87.\nPharaoh threatened the believers with crucifixion to get revenge on them, but Allah dealt with him in kind. Explain.\nوَإِذۡ وَٰعَدۡنَا مُوسَىٰٓ أَرۡبَعِينَ لَيۡلَةٗ ثُمَّ ٱتَّخَذۡتُمُ ٱلۡعِجۡلَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦ وَأَنتُمۡ ظَٰلِمُونَ ٥١\nNight is mentioned because the best communing with Allah is during nighttime. Al-Biqai: 1/133.\n(nights) are mentioned rather than \"days\" for communing with Allah. Why?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوۡمِهِۦ يَٰقَوۡمِ إِنَّكُمۡ ظَلَمۡتُمۡ أَنفُسَكُم بِٱتِّخَاذِكُمُ ٱلۡعِجۡلَ فَتُوبُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ بَارِئِكُمۡ\nThe grave sin that they had committed by which they wronged themselves is what Allah mentioned about their apostacy by worshiping a calf after Moses (u) left them. Al-Tabari:2/72.\nThe absence of scholars and righteous people in society may lead to its deviance. Explain.\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوۡمِهِۦ يَٰقَوۡمِ إِنَّكُمۡ ظَلَمۡتُمۡ أَنفُسَكُم بِٱتِّخَاذِكُمُ ٱلۡعِجۡلَ\nYou have made yourselves subservient to a useless (inanimate object) to which your own selves are superior. This is the worst wrongdoing, for it is not fitting for one to be subservient and worship someone like him, then how about worshiping what is less than that, an animal! Not only that, but a gold metal object that resembles an animal. Al-Biqai: 1/134.\nIgnorance about the Lordship of Allah is the worst kind of ignorance. Explain.\nوَظَلَّلۡنَا عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡغَمَامَ وَأَنزَلۡنَا عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡمَنَّ وَٱلسَّلۡوَىٰۖ\nWhen Allah, the Almighty, mentioned the punishments from that He had averted from them, He began to remind them of the blessings He had bestowed upon them, saying: (We shaded you with clouds). Ibn Kathir: 1/90.\nWhat is the link between this verse and the preceding verses?\nوَظَلَّلۡنَا عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡغَمَامَ وَأَنزَلۡنَا عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡمَنَّ وَٱلسَّلۡوَىٰۖ كُلُواْ مِن طَيِّبَٰتِ مَا رَزَقۡنَٰكُمۡۚ وَمَا ظَلَمُونَا وَلَٰكِن كَانُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡ يَظۡلِمُونَ ٥٧\nThe manna and quails would come down to them in sufficient quantities to nourish them, (Eat from the good things with which We have provided you), that is, provision the like of which even those who dwell in cities and live a life of luxury do not have. But they were not grateful for this blessing, and continued to be hardhearted and committed many sins. Al-Saadi: 49.\nWhat is the reason for the successive and hard punishments on Children of Israel?\nوَمَا ظَلَمُونَا وَلَٰكِن كَانُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡ يَظۡلِمُونَ ٥٧\nIn this verse, the expression of wrongdoing is stated in the past tense and past continuous forms to indicate their persistence in wrongdoing and their continuation thereof. Al-Alusi: 1/264.\nIn this verse, the wrongdoing of Children of Israel is expressed in past tense and past continuous forms. Why?\nwords\nفَرَقنَاWe divided\nبَارِئِكُمOne Who brought you into existence\nالغَمَامَClouds\nالمَنَّA kind of sweet gum"],[9,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nEnsure, today, that you perform the confirmed Sunnah prayers, and maintain them continuously.\nRead the correct words and supplications mentioned in prayer from one of the books on the description of prayer that are authenticated, and correct any mistakes you may have.\nRemind your family of a blessing which they have and belittle while many families do not have.\nguid\nBeware that the door of mercy and good deeds is opened for you and you waste it due to your carelessness.\nDo not belittle a provision from Allah for you, lest He replaces it with something else that looks good in appearance, but is bad for you.\nHumiliation, poverty and incurring the wrath of Allah are some consequences of committing sins.\nrefl\nوَإِذۡ قُلۡنَا ٱدۡخُلُواْ هَٰذِهِ ٱلۡقَرۡيَةَ فَكُلُواْ مِنۡهَا حَيۡثُ شِئۡتُمۡ رَغَدٗا وَٱدۡخُلُواْ ٱلۡبَابَ سُجَّدٗا وَقُولُواْ حِطَّةٞ\nIn summary: They were commanded to submit to Allah at the time of conquest in deed and word, confess their sins, seek forgiveness for them, and be grateful for Allah's blessings. That is why Prophet Muhammad (r) showed humbleness in victory. It was narrated that on the day of the conquest of Makkah, he entered from the upper Thaniyah (a mountain pass to Makkah), and he was so humble to his Lord that his beard was touching the hump of his camel in gratitude to Allah. Then, when he entered the city, he washed himself and prayed eight Rak'as. Ibn Kathir: 1/94.\nWhat should Muslims do at the time of victory?\nقَالَ أَتَسۡتَبۡدِلُونَ ٱلَّذِي هُوَ أَدۡنَىٰ بِٱلَّذِي هُوَ خَيۡرٌۚ ٱهۡبِطُواْ مِصۡرٗا فَإِنَّ لَكُم مَّا سَأَلۡتُمۡۗ وَضُرِبَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلذِّلَّةُ وَٱلۡمَسۡكَنَةُ وَبَآءُو بِغَضَبٖ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِۗ\nThis contains a threat to this Muslim nation due to what has prevailed among some of them who, like the Children of Israel, replace what is less in meaning from the forbidden and ambiguous with what is higher in meaning from the good. Al-Biqai: 1/149.\nWhat lessons can Muslims learn from what happened to the Children of Israel?\nوَضُرِبَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلذِّلَّةُ وَٱلۡمَسۡكَنَةُ\nSince their behavior was the greatest evidence of their lack of patience and their contempt for the commands and blessings of Allah, He requited them with an appropriate punishment; He says, (They were struck with humiliation) that could be seen on their physical appearance, (and poverty) in their hearts. Al-Saadi: 53.\nWhy were humiliation and poverty considered an appropriate punishment for the sins of Children of Israel?\nوَضُرِبَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلذِّلَّةُ وَٱلۡمَسۡكَنَةُ\nThe meaning of the permanence of humiliation and poverty of the Jews is that they lost their courage and bravery, and the signs of poverty and need became apparent on them despite the abundance of what Allah had bestowed upon them; however, when they grew tired of it, it became like nothing to them, and therefore greed became a permanent characteristic of theirs. Ibn Ashur: 1/528.\nGreed and avarice are Jewish traits. How does the above verse indicate this fact?\nوَيَقۡتُلُونَ ٱلنَّبِيِّۧنَ بِغَيۡرِ ٱلۡحَقِّۗ ذَٰلِكَ بِمَا عَصَواْ وَّكَانُواْ يَعۡتَدُونَ ٦١\nThat was because (they disobeyed) by committing sins and (were transgressing) against the servants of Allah, for one sin leads to another. Heedlessness leads to a minor sin that leads to a major one, which then leads to various types of innovation, disbelief and other things. We ask Allah to keep us safe from all trials. Al-Saadi: 53.\nWhen a heedless person disregards minor sins, they will lead him to major sins, then to disbelief. Explain.\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ يَكۡفُرُونَ بِٔايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ وَيَقۡتُلُونَ ٱلنَّبِيِّۧنَ بِغَيۡرِ ٱلۡحَقِّۗ ذَٰلِكَ بِمَا عَصَواْ وَّكَانُواْ يَعۡتَدُونَ ٦١\nAddiction to committing sins leads one deeper into them, moving from a minor sin to a major one. Ibn Ashur: 1/530.\nWhat can you infer from the movement of the Children of Israel from minor sins to disbelief and killing of their Prophets?\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ كَانُواْ يَكۡفُرُونَ بِٔايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ وَيَقۡتُلُونَ ٱلنَّبِيِّۧنَ بِغَيۡرِ ٱلۡحَقِّۗ ذَٰلِكَ بِمَا عَصَواْ وَّكَانُواْ يَعۡتَدُونَ ٦١\nThe meaning is that what led them to disbelieve in the signs of Allah and kill the prophets was their previous disobedience, aggression, and crossing of the limits set by Allah, as one sin leads to another. Al-Alusi: 1/277.\nWhat led the Jews to disbelieve in the signs of Allah and kill the Prophets?\nwords\nوَقُولُوا حِطَّةٌ\"Say: \"Relieve us of our sins\nرِجزًاTorment\nوَلاَ تَعثَواDo not spread corruption\nو باؤواWent through"],[10,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nGet up early, today, to attend to your religious and worldly matters, and try to be more diligent, then reflect on the difference in results.\nShare a message in which you remind those around you that committing a sin with a deceitful intention incurs the wrath of Allah more than a direct plain sin.\nShare a message in which you remind the society that Allah Knows the difference between false piety and truthful one.\nguid\nA Muslim must hold firm to his religion and should not forsake any of it when encountering hardships or calamities.\nThe punishment that strike others is an admonition for you.\nRemember Allah's favor and grace upon you by giving you the religion of Islam, and be grateful to Him, for if it was not for Him, you would have been among the losers in this life and the Hereafter.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَٱلَّذِينَ هَادُواْ وَٱلنَّصَٰرَىٰ وَٱلصَّٰبِٔينَ مَنۡ ءَامَنَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحٗا فَلَهُمۡ أَجۡرُهُمۡ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ وَلَا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ٦٢\nThis is the Quran's style; if baseless assumptions come to the minds of some people through some verses, they will always find what clarify the matter because it is a revelation from the One Who knows all things before they happen, and Whose mercy encompasses all things. The way in which this may be clarified -and Allah knows best- is that when the Quran mentions the Children of Israel and censures them for their sins and abhorrent actions, that may give the impression that all of the Israelites are subject to this condemnation. Hence, in this verse, the Creator highlighted those who were not included in this condemnation. As mentioning of the Children of Israel in particular may also give the impression that this ruling applies to them only, Allah states a general rule that applies to all those other groups to clarify the truth and dispel confusion and doubt. Al-Saadi: 54.\nThis verse come after mentioning the abhorrent actions of Children of Israel. Why?\nوَإِذۡ أَخَذۡنَا مِيثَٰقَكُمۡ وَرَفَعۡنَا فَوۡقَكُمُ ٱلطُّورَ خُذُواْ مَآ ءَاتَيۡنَٰكُم بِقُوَّةٖ\n(Hold firmly), with seriousness and diligence, not laziness or heedlessness. Al-Alusi: 1/281.\nWhat does (holding firmly to what Allah reveals) mean?\nوَلَقَدۡ عَلِمۡتُمُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱعۡتَدَوۡاْ مِنكُمۡ فِي ٱلسَّبۡتِ فَقُلۡنَا لَهُمۡ كُونُواْ قِرَدَةً خَٰسِٔينَ ٦٥\nEven though the digging [of holes to catch the fish] was done on Friday, Allah considered this as a breaking of the Sabbath covenant because the effect of their action occurred on Saturday when the fish entered the holes. Ibn Ashur: 1/544.\nWhy was the Jewish transgression considered a breaking of the Sabbath covenant even though the digging was done on Friday?\nفَجَعَلۡنَٰهَا نَكَٰلٗا لِّمَا بَيۡنَ يَدَيۡهَا وَمَا خَلۡفَهَا وَمَوۡعِظَةٗ لِّلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٦٦\nBut it is only a useful admonition for the righteous who fear Allah; others do not benefit from the signs. Al-Saadi: 54.\nWhy was this considered an admonition for the righteous only?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوۡمِهِۦٓ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَأۡمُرُكُمۡ أَن تَذۡبَحُواْ بَقَرَةٗۖ\nAl-Mawardi said: They were commanded to slaughter a cow and not another animal because it was of the same species as the calf they had worshipped, so that what was previously revered to them would be demeaned in their eyes, and to reveal by their response what lies in their hearts with regard to worshiping the calf. Al-Qurtubi: 2/177.\nAllah Commanded them to slaughter a cow. What is the wisdom behind that?\nقَالُوٓاْ أَتَتَّخِذُنَا هُزُوٗاۖ قَالَ أَعُوذُ بِٱللَّهِ أَنۡ أَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلۡجَٰهِلِينَ ٦٧\nMoses (u) was seeking refuge with Allah because mocking is unfitting for wise and virtuous men let alone a Messenger of Allah. Mocking is worse than joking because it involves disdain and contempt for the listeners. Moreover, mocking in a speech to a public gathering is totally inappropriate, and therefore Moses disowned it. Ibn Ashur: 1/548.\nMoses (u) answered by saying, (I seek refuge with Allah from being among the ignorant). Why?\nقَالُواْ ٱدۡعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّن لَّنَا مَا هِيَۚ قَالَ إِنَّهُۥ يَقُولُ إِنَّهَا بَقَرَةٞ لَّا فَارِضٞ وَلَا بِكۡرٌ عَوَانُۢ بَيۡنَ ذَٰلِكَۖ فَٱفۡعَلُواْ مَا تُؤۡمَرُونَ ٦٨ قَالُواْ ٱدۡعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّن لَّنَا مَا لَوۡنُهَاۚ قَالَ إِنَّهُۥ يَقُولُ إِنَّهَا بَقَرَةٞ صَفۡرَآءُ فَاقِعٞ لَّوۡنُهَا تَسُرُّ ٱلنَّٰظِرِينَ ٦٩\nHad they slaughtered a cow, any cow, it would have sufficed; instead, they made the matter difficult, and this is why Allah made it even more difficult for them. Finally, they found this particular cow with someone who had no cows but this one, and so he asked for gold filling its skin. So, they paid, took the cow and slaughtered it. Ibn Kathir: 1/103.\nWhat are the consequences of being extreme in religion?\nwords\nوَالصَّابِئِينَPeople who worship Allah without specific Sharia\nفَارِضٌOld in age\nبِكرٌYoung in age\nعَوَانٌBetween old and young\nفَاقِعٌBright yellow"],[11,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\n(The balance of heart is in its solitude). Perform an act of worship alone by yourself, for Allah knows what you conceal and reveal.\nParticipate in something that softens your heart such as washing or burying of the dead, visiting a hospital emergency room, or spending time with a devout worshiper.\nShare a message or an article about some examples of current hypocrisy.\nguid\nResponding to the commands of Allah after much arguing is a sign of stubbornness or false piety.\nAllah is Capable of exposing your hidden sins, so beware of the presence of His knowledge.\nSins are the cause for hardening of the hearts.\nrefl\nوَإِنَّآ إِن شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ لَمُهۡتَدُونَ\nHad they not made this exception: (And indeed we, if Allah wills, will be guided), they would have never been able to find the cow at all. Ibn Kathir: 1/104.\nWhat benefit did Moses' people gain by making this exception?\nقَالُواْ ٱلۡـَٰٔنَ جِئۡتَ بِٱلۡحَقِّۚ\nThey said this because of their ignorance, for the truth had come to them from the outset. If they had gone and fetched any cow, they would have achieved their objective, but they made it difficult for themselves by asking too many questions, so Allah made it difficult for them. Al-Saadi: 55.\nWhat does the saying of Moses' people indicate, (Now you have come with the truth)?\nفَذَبَحُوهَا وَمَا كَادُواْ يَفۡعَلُونَ ٧١\nThey almost had not done so), perhaps because of their disobedience and questioning, or because the cow's price was very high. It was narrated that the cow belonged to an orphan, and they had to pay as much as its weight in gold, or because a cow with these descriptions was very rare. Had they gone and fetched any cow, it would have sufficed, but they made it difficult for themselves so Allah made it difficult for them. Ibn Juzay: 1/70.\nA person's false piety brings him hardship as opposed to truthful piety. Explain.\nثُمَّ قَسَتۡ قُلُوبُكُم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ ذَٰلِكَ فَهِيَ كَٱلۡحِجَارَةِ أَوۡ أَشَدُّ قَسۡوَةٗۚ\nThen, Allah describes their hardheartedness as being like a stone, which is harder than iron, because iron and lead melt when they are exposed to fire but stones do not. Al-Saadi: 55.\nWhy are their hearts compared to a stone and not an iron for example?\nثُمَّ قَسَتۡ قُلُوبُكُم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ ذَٰلِكَ فَهِيَ كَٱلۡحِجَارَةِ أَوۡ أَشَدُّ قَسۡوَةٗۚ\nThe strength of the heart is favorable trait, unlike hardness of the heart, which is censured. The heart should be strong without violence and soft without weakness. Ibn Taimyah: 2/243.\nWhat is the difference between strength and hardness of the heart?\nوَإِنَّ مِنَ ٱلۡحِجَارَةِ لَمَا يَتَفَجَّرُ مِنۡهُ ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُۚ وَإِنَّ مِنۡهَا لَمَا يَشَّقَّقُ فَيَخۡرُجُ مِنۡهُ ٱلۡمَآءُۚ وَإِنَّ مِنۡهَا لَمَا يَهۡبِطُ مِنۡ خَشْيَةِ ٱللَّهِ ٧٤\nSome stones are more beneficial than your hearts because stones fall down and water bursts from them. Mujahid said: \"No stone falls from the top of a mountain, nor does a river bursts out of a rock, nor does water flow from it except out of fear of Allah. This is revealed in the Quran.\" Al-Qurtubi: 2/208.\nFrom the above verse, some stones be more beneficial than hardened hearts. Explain.\nأَفَتَطۡمَعُونَ أَن يُؤۡمِنُواْ لَكُمۡ وَقَدۡ كَانَ فَرِيقٞ مِّنۡهُمۡ يَسۡمَعُونَ كَلَٰمَ ٱللَّهِ ثُمَّ يُحَرِّفُونَهُۥ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا عَقَلُوهُ وَهُمۡ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٧٥\n(After understanding it) after knowing and comprehending. This is a rebuke to the Jews [who were at Prophet Muhammad's (r) time] because they followed their forefathers in their rejection of truth and stubbornness. Moreover, it indicates that anyone who knows the truth yet he disputes it, is far from the right guidance since he knew Allah's reward and punishment but that did not deter him from his stubbornness. Al-Qurtubi: 2/213.\nWho is closer to the right guidance: An ignorant person or a knowledgeable person with stubbornness?\nwords\nلاَ ذَلُولٌNot tamed for working in the farm\nمُسَلَّمَةٌWithout defects\nلاَشِيَةَWithout spots of a different color\nفَادَّارَأتُمSwapped accusation of murder among yourselves"],[12,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nIn light of this verse, share a message about the importance of reforming one's inner self.\nStart a program, today, to understand the verses of the Quran by reading one of its simple interpretations, so you will be among those who understand the words of Allah.\nSelect one of these acts of worship and implement it today so you will be of those who practice the Quran, then see how your heart feels afterward.\nguid\nRemember that Allah knows what you conceal and reveal, hence ensure that He sees only good from you in both cases.\nDo not underestimate the divine punishment since that leads to hardening of the heart and more sins.\nAllah combines His right with the rights of parents, so do not neglect your parents' rights.\nrefl\nوَمِنۡهُمۡ أُمِّيُّونَ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ إِلَّآ أَمَانِيَّ وَإِنۡ هُمۡ إِلَّا يَظُنُّونَ ٧٨\n(Except wishful thinking): Reciting [the Torah] without understanding. Ibn Juzay: 1/72.\nHow are we to understand this verse as a condemnation of those who read the Quran without understanding?\nوَمِنۡهُمۡ أُمِّيُّونَ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ إِلَّآ أَمَانِيَّ وَإِنۡ هُمۡ إِلَّا يَظُنُّونَ ٧٨\nThis is a description of one who does not understand nor adhere to the words of Allah but rather limits himself to reciting it. Alhasan Al-Basri said: \"The Quran was revealed to be acted upon, but they settled for its recitation only.\" Ibn Taimyah: 1/247.\nNeglecting to reflect and adhere to the teachings of the Quran is censured by the Quran. Explain.\nفَوَيۡلٞ لِّلَّذِينَ يَكۡتُبُونَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ بِأَيۡدِيهِمۡ ثُمَّ يَقُولُونَ هَٰذَا مِنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ لِيَشۡتَرُواْ بِهِۦ ثَمَنٗا قَلِيلٗاۖ\nThey did that knowingly, (in order to trade it for a small price). All of this world, from beginning to end, is a small price. They made their falsehood a means of snatching what is in people's hands. Thus, they wronged the people on two counts: They confused them with regard to their religion and took their wealth unlawfully, by the worst of means, which is worse than those who take people's wealth by force or by stealing and so on. Al-Saadi: 56.\nWhoever distorts the text of the book or its meaning is unjust in two ways. Explain.\nوَإِذۡ أَخَذۡنَا مِيثَٰقَ بَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ لَا تَعۡبُدُونَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَ وَبِٱلۡوَٰلِدَيۡنِ إِحۡسَانٗا\nWe command them to be kind to parents. Allah combines being good to one's parents with Tawhīd because the first development in the womb comes from Allah, and the second, which involves upbringing and teaching, is at the hands of one's parents, which is why Allah, the Almighty, links thanking them with thanking Him. Al-Qurtubi: 2/229.\nAllah combines His right with the rights of parents. Why?\nوَبِٱلۡوَٰلِدَيۡنِ إِحۡسَانٗا وَذِي ٱلۡقُرۡبَىٰ وَٱلۡيَتَٰمَىٰ وَٱلۡمَسَٰكِينِ وَقُولُواْ لِلنَّاسِ حُسۡنٗا\nAfter commanding His servants to be kind to people, Allah commands them to say good words to them, thereby combining two types of kindness: Good speech and good deeds. Ibn Kathir: 1/115.\nAllah mentions good speech after mentioning good deeds. Why?\nوَقُولُواْ لِلنَّاسِ حُسۡنٗا\nAllah enjoins speaking good words to all people because it is the measure by which all people can be treated. When they speak kindly to people, it reflects goodness in their hearts toward them. Ibn Ashur: 1/583.\nAllah enjoins speaking good words to all people. Why?\nوَقُولُواْ لِلنَّاسِ حُسۡنٗا\nIt is speaking softly to people and behaving in good manners toward them. Al-Baghawi: 1/72.\nExplain the virtue of kind speech and its importance according to Islamic teachings.\nwords\nأُمِيُّونَIlliterate (unable to read or write)\nأَمَانِيَّRecitation, or lies they gathered from their scholars\nفَوَيلٌWoe and destruction\nمِيثَاقَA confirmed covenant\nحُسنًاGood, kind words"],[13,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nSeek to free a captive or a prisoner by interceding, providing financial assistance or by a sincere supplication during nighttime or at an hour of response.\nAsk for advice from a friend, and when given one, accept it as long as it is true, and do not reject it because it does not suit your desire.\nSay, \"I am pleased with Allah as my Lord, with Muhammad (r) as a Messenger of Allah and with Islam as my religion.\"\nguid\nReflect on how Allah describes their killing of one another as: (killing yourselves) because a believer with his brother are like one soul; they share happiness and sorrow.\nThe belief in Allah entails contentment with His whole religion. Accepting part and rejecting another is a form of hypocrisy. Allah forbids.\nJews are Jews are not trustworthy with the Torah in their hands, so how can they be trusted with other treaties and covenants?\nrefl\nوَإِن يَأۡتُوكُمۡ أُسَٰرَىٰ تُفَٰدُوهُمۡ\nIt was reported that Prophet Muhammad (r) ransomed captives and ordered their release. This was the practice of Muslims, and consensus was reached on this issue. It is mandatory to ransom captives using public funds from the public treasury. If it is not paid, then it is an obligation on all Muslims, but if it is fulfilled by some of them, it will suffice. Al-Qurtubi: 2/242.\nWhat is our duty toward Muslim captives around the world?\nأَفَتُؤۡمِنُونَ بِبَعۡضِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَتَكۡفُرُونَ بِبَعۡضٖۚ\nThis presents the strongest evidence that faith requires acting upon commands and heeding prohibitions, and that ordained deeds are part of faith. Al-Saadi: 58.\nUsing this verse, how do you respond to someone who claims to have faith but does not act?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱشۡتَرَوُاْ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۖ\nAllah states the reason why they disbelieved in part of the Scripture and believed in another: (Those are the ones who have bought the life of this world [in exchange] for the Hereafter). Al-Saadi: 58.\nWhat is the reason that some people believe in part of the Scripture and disbelieve in another?\nوَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَا مُوسَى ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَقَفَّيۡنَا مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦ بِٱلرُّسُلِۖ وَءَاتَيۡنَا عِيسَى ٱبۡنَ مَرۡيَمَ ٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ وَأَيَّدۡنَٰهُ بِرُوحِ ٱلۡقُدُسِۗ\nStrengthening with the Holy Spirit (Gabriel) applies to all those who support the Messengers against the disbelievers whether polytheists or people of the Book (Jews and Christians). Ibn Taimyah: 1/268.\nWho does Allah strengthen with the Holy Spirit?\nأَفَكُلَّمَا جَآءَكُمۡ رَسُولُۢ بِمَا لَا تَهۡوَىٰٓ أَنفُسُكُمُ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرۡتُمۡ\nIn the Arabic text, the word used for (desire) is \"Hawa\", which means \"falling into something.\" It is called that because desires eventually make a person fall into Hellfire; therefore, the word, \"Hawa\" is used only for what is false and without virtue. Al-Qurtubi: 2/245.\nTo where does \"Hawa\" lead its follower?\nوَقَالُواْ قُلُوبُنَا غُلۡفُۢ بَل لَّعَنَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِكُفۡرِهِمۡ فَقَلِيلٗا مَّا يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٨٨\nThey told Prophet Muhammad (r) that their hearts were wrapped by impenetrable cover preventing his teaching from reaching them in order to make him despair of their acceptance and completely cut off his hope for them, so Allah, the Almighty distanced them from His mercy. Al-Alusi: 1/318.\nWhat did the Jews mean by saying: (Our hearts are wrapped)? And what was their punishment?\nوَقَالُواْ قُلُوبُنَا غُلۡفُۢ بَل لَّعَنَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِكُفۡرِهِمۡ فَقَلِيلٗا مَّا يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٨٨\n(But, in fact), Allah repudiates their claim of \"wrapped hearts\", rather (Allah has cursed them), the greatest King has expelled them from accepting the truth, for they are not worthy of guidance after Allah had created them on the true nature (Fitrah) without wrapped hearts. Cursing entails banishment morally and physically. Al-Biqai: 1/182.\nAllah cursed them and expelled them from His mercy. Why?\nwords\nتُفَادُوهُمSeek to liberate them from captivity\nخِزيٌHumiliation and disgrace\nوَقَفَّينَاSent in succession\nغُلفٌWrapped"],[14,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from transgression and envy.\nAsk Allah Almighty to grant you modesty, and train yourself to be modest, for it is the key to goodness, just as arrogance is the key to evil.\nKeep saying this supplication: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment.\" When Allah became angry with the Jews, He exposed their faults and secrets to all people.\nguid\nEnvying others for Allah's favor upon them results in Allah's wrath and humiliating punishment.\nYou must hold on to your religion strongly, for a strong believer who holds on to his religion is better than a weak one.\nInsisting on stubbornness leads to it being absorbed into the heart of the stubborn person and becoming as if it were a reality for him.\nrefl\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُم مَّا عَرَفُواْ كَفَرُواْ بِهِۦۚ فَلَعۡنَةُ ٱللَّهِ عَلَى ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٨٩\nTheir disbelief was merely due to stubbornness, which is the result of envy, not ignorance. This is more severe in its condemnation, because an ignorant person may be excused. Al-Alusi: 1/322.\nWhy did the Jews disbelieve in the Message of Prophet Muhammad (r)?\nبِئۡسَمَا ٱشۡتَرَوۡاْ بِهِۦٓ أَنفُسَهُمۡ أَن يَكۡفُرُواْ بِمَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ بَغۡيًا أَن يُنَزِّلَ ٱللَّهُ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦ عَلَىٰ مَن يَشَآءُ مِنۡ عِبَادِهِۦۖ فَبَآءُو بِغَضَبٍ عَلَىٰ غَضَبٖۚ وَلِلۡكَٰفِرِينَ عَذَابٞ مُّهِينٞ ٩٠\nSince their disbelief was caused by their transgression and envy, which stem from arrogance, they were met with humiliation and degradation in this world and the Hereafter. Ibn Kathir: 120.\nThe recompense fits the deed. Explain in light of the this verse.\nفَبَآءُو بِغَضَبٍ عَلَىٰ غَضَبٖۚ\nHence, Allah cursed them and was angry with them. They have incurred his wrath upon wrath because of their ample disbelief and continuous doubt and shirk (associating partners with Allah). Al-Saadi: 59.\nWhy did the Jews deserve wrath upon another?\nوَهُوَ ٱلۡحَقُّ مُصَدِّقٗا لِّمَا مَعَهُمۡۗ\nSo, why do you believe in what was revealed to you and disbelieve in its equivalent? Can this be anything other than bias and following whims and desires? Al-Saadi: 59.\nThe Quran shows that the reason for their disbelief in the Quran is bias and following whims. Explain in light of this verse.\nقُلۡ فَلِمَ تَقۡتُلُونَ أَنۢبِيَآءَ ٱللَّهِ مِن قَبۡلُ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ٩١\nAdding the word (Prophets) to Allah's Holy Name is a great honor, and a sign for them that one who came with a message from Allah should be revered and supported, not killed. Al-Alusi: 1/324.\nWhat is the significance of adding the name of a creature to the Name of Allah?\nوَإِذۡ أَخَذۡنَا مِيثَٰقَكُمۡ وَرَفَعۡنَا فَوۡقَكُمُ ٱلطُّورَ خُذُواْ مَآ ءَاتَيۡنَٰكُم بِقُوَّةٖ وَٱسۡمَعُواْۖ\n(And raised over you the mount), We made the great mountain a deterrent to you from being content to remain in the depths of ignorance, and to elevate you to the pinnacle of knowledge. Whoever hears but did not accept is as one who never heard. (And listen), or else, We will bury you with it while it is sufficient for others the use of a stick or a whip to stimulate them to learn. Al-Biqai: 1/198.\nDisciplining the stubborn in accordance with the limit of his stubbornness. To what limit the disciplining of the Jews reach?\nخُذُواْ مَآ ءَاتَيۡنَٰكُم بِقُوَّةٖ وَٱسۡمَعُواْۖ\nMeaning: Listen to accept, obey, and respond. Al-Saadi: 59.\nWhat kind of listening to the Holy Quran does Allah Almighty, want us to do?\nwords\nيَستَفتِحُونَCounted on the coming Prophet to defeat the polytheists\nفباؤواWent through"],[15,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nMake a plan for your life in which a major righteous deed is included that will make you long for the Hereafter.\nAsk Allah to grant you a good end of life and the joy of meeting Him, without any harm or misleading trials.\nReview the list of your collogues and friends, and try to add others whom you think are allies of Allah.\nguid\nThe more sins a servant commits, the more he becomes oblivious to death and its remembrance.\nWhoever is loved by Allah, the angels of Allah will love him too.\nBeware of becoming an enemy to the allies of Allah, for that would make Allah an enemy to you.\nrefl\nقُلۡ إِن كَانَتۡ لَكُمُ ٱلدَّارُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةُ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ خَالِصَةٗ مِّن دُونِ ٱلنَّاسِ فَتَمَنَّوُاْ ٱلۡمَوۡتَ إِن كُنتُمۡ صَٰدِقِينَ ٩٤\nBecause whoever believes that he is among the people of Paradise, death is more beloved to him than life in this world since he will attain of the bliss of Paradise, and be relieved of the harm of worldly life. Al-Qurtubi: 2/257.\nAllah Commands the Jews to wish for death. Why?\nقُلۡ إِن كَانَتۡ لَكُمُ ٱلدَّارُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةُ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ خَالِصَةٗ مِّن دُونِ ٱلنَّاسِ فَتَمَنَّوُاْ ٱلۡمَوۡتَ إِن كُنتُمۡ صَٰدِقِينَ ٩٤\nWishing for death can be a sign of the servant's good relation with his Lord and his hope to meet Him. The more the soul is averse to death, the weaker its attainment of the knowledge by which it finds comfort in its Lord, so it longs to meet Him and loves that. Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him, and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him. Al-Biqai: 1/200.\nWhat does it mean to wish to meet Allah?\nوَلَتَجِدَنَّهُمۡ أَحۡرَصَ ٱلنَّاسِ عَلَىٰ حَيَوٰةٖ وَمِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَشۡرَكُواْۚ يَوَدُّ أَحَدُهُمۡ لَوۡ يُعَمَّرُ أَلۡفَ سَنَةٖ وَمَا هُوَ بِمُزَحۡزِحِهِۦ مِنَ ٱلۡعَذَابِ أَن يُعَمَّرَۗ وَٱللَّهُ بَصِيرُۢ بِمَا يَعۡمَلُونَ ٩٦\nAllah censured them for being desperate to remain in this life in any condition, knowing that -even if it was the worst condition- it will still be better than what is waiting for them after death. Al-Biqai: 1/202.\nWhat is the reason for their clinging to this life in any condition?\nوَمَا هُوَ بِمُزَحۡزِحِهِۦ مِنَ ٱلۡعَذَابِ أَن يُعَمَّرَۗ وَٱللَّهُ بَصِيرُۢ بِمَا يَعۡمَلُونَ ٩٦\n(It would not remove him in the least): It would not save him (From the [coming] Punishment): From Hellfire in the Hereafter. (That he should be granted life), means that his lengthy lifetime would not save him from punishment. Al-Baghawi: 1/79.\nDoes longevity save a person from Allah's punishment?\nقُلۡ مَن كَانَ عَدُوّٗا لِّـجِبۡرِيلَ فَإِنَّهُۥ نَزَّلَهُۥ عَلَىٰ قَلۡبِكَ بِإِذۡنِ ٱللَّهِ\nThe heart is mentioned because it is the place of the intellect, knowledge and it is the device by which a person comprehends information. Al-Qurtubi: 2/262.\nIn light of this verse, explain the importance of the heart.\nفَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَدُوّٞ لِّلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٩٨\nWhoever takes an ally of Allah as an enemy, he has taken Allah as an enemy, and whoever treats Allah as an enemy, he shall be Allah's enemy. Whoever is an enemy of Allah, will be a loser in this life and the Hereafter. Ibn Kathir: 1/127.\nWhat is the risk in taking the allies of Allah as enemies?\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمۡ رَسُولٞ مِّنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ مُصَدِّقٞ لِّمَا مَعَهُمۡ نَبَذَ فَرِيقٞ مِّنَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ كِتَٰبَ ٱللَّهِ وَرَآءَ ظُهُورِهِمۡ كَأَنَّهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ١٠١\nSufyan bin Uyaynah said: They enclosed it [Torah] in silk and brocade and adorned it with gold and silver, but they did not adhere to its teachings; that is the meaning of throwing it behind their back. Al-Baghawi: 1/82.\nWhat is the meaning of true honoring and true rejection of the Book of Allah (The Holy Quran)?\nwords\nبمزحزحہRemoves him\nنَبَذَهُThrew it away"],[16,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from the evil of an envier when he envies, and from the evil of the blowers in knots.\nSeek to mend the relation between two people, especially spouses, as the devil and his soldiers seek to cause corruption between people and spouses, so be a good mediator.\nWarn the community of the presence of sorcerers, and explain their threat and the necessity of cooperation to ward off their evil.\nguid\nA magician is a disbeliever; learning and using magic is prohibited.\nWhoever clings to Allah, Allah will suffice him from all evils.\nEnvy is an influential factor in the relationship between the People of the Scripture and Muslims.\nrefl\nوَمَا كَفَرَ سُلَيۡمَٰنُ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينَ كَفَرُواْ يُعَلِّمُونَ ٱلنَّاسَ ٱلسِّحۡرَ\nBlack magic or witchcraft is achieved by getting closer to the devil by committing abhorrent acts verbally such as recitation of words that contain \"shirk\" (associating partners with Allah), praising the devil and harnessing his influence; and by action such as worshiping the planets, committing crimes and other immoral acts. Al-Alusi: 1/338.\nLearning black magic can only be achieved through shirk and disbelief, Explain.\nوَمَا كَفَرَ سُلَيۡمَٰنُ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينَ كَفَرُواْ يُعَلِّمُونَ ٱلنَّاسَ ٱلسِّحۡرَ\nJust as the angels only help good people who resemble them in their persistence in worship and drawing closer to Allah in word and deed, so the devils only help evil people who resemble them in their wickedness and impurity in word, deed and belief. In this way, a magician is distinguished from a Prophet and an ally of Allah. Al-Alusi: 1/338.\nWhat kind of relationships exist between mankind and each of these two beings: Angels and devils?\nوَمَا هُم بِضَآرِّينَ بِهِۦ مِنۡ أَحَدٍ إِلَّا بِإِذۡنِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nIn this and similar verses, it is stated that no matter how powerful the causes may be, they are still subject to the divine will and decree. Causes are not independent in their effects. Al-Saadi: 61.\nWhat is the right view of a Muslim on the issue of causes?\nوَيَتَعَلَّمُونَ مَا يَضُرُّهُمۡ وَلَا يَنفَعُهُمۡۚ\nThey learn the magic that harms their faith and does not benefit them in the Hereafter. Al-Tabari: 2/450.\nWhat is meant by (did not benefit) in the above verse?\nوَلَقَدۡ عَلِمُواْ لَمَنِ ٱشۡتَرَىٰهُ مَا لَهُۥ فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ مِنۡ خَلَٰقٖۚ وَلَبِئۡسَ مَا شَرَوۡاْ بِهِۦٓ أَنفُسَهُمۡۚ لَوۡ كَانُواْ يَعۡلَمُونَ ١٠٢\nMagic will not benefit the one who practices it in the Hereafter and will not bring him closer to Allah. Whoever chose it, will have no share in the Hereafter because it is based on \"shirk\", lies and oppression of others. A magician's intention is based on oppressing others and committing immoral acts. Ibn Taimyah: 2/287.\nMagic does not benefit one who practices it nor bring him closer to Allah. Why?\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّهُمۡ ءَامَنُواْ وَٱتَّقَوۡاْ لَمَثُوبَةٞ مِّنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ خَيۡرٞۚ لَّوۡ كَانُواْ يَعۡلَمُونَ ١٠٣\nAllah says, (A better reward from Allah), not \"Allah's reward\" even though it is abbreviated to indicate that even a small reward from Allah in the permanent Hereafter is much better than a bigger one in this mortal world; then how so when Allah's reward is abundant and everlasting? Al-Alusi: 1/347.\nAllah says, (A better reward from Allah), not \"Allah's reward.\" Why?\nيٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَقُولُواْ رَٰعِنَا وَقُولُواْ ٱنظُرۡنَا وَٱسۡمَعُواْ\nWhen Muslims addressed the Messenger (r) as he was teaching them about their religion, they would say: Ra'ina, (consider our situation), using the word in its correct meaning. The Jews, however, gave the same word an offensive meaning; they took advantage of this opportunity to address the Messenger (r) with this word, intending the offensive meaning. Therefore, Allah commanded the believers not to use this word to put an end to this situation. This proves that something permissible may be disallowed when it becomes a means that leads to unlawful things. Al-Saadi: 61.\nDeduce from the above verse an Islamic etiquette for addressing others.\nwords\nاشتَرَاهُChose it\nخَلاَقٍA share (Portion)\nرَاعِنَا(ﷺ) A word (with negative connotation) used by Jews when addressing the Prophet"],[17,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from the evil of envy, and beware of envious people.\nShare a message or write an article explaining that many Jews and Christians hope to turn Muslims away from their faith, as mentioned in the Quran.\nPerform the five daily prayers on time.\nguid\nAbrogation is a form of progression in Islamic legislation, and it is a mercy from Allah to the believers.\nBe certain that what is ordained by Allah is all good, and what is forbidden by Him is all evil.\nPardoning and forgiving are great traits of Muslims, whether toward Muslims or non-Muslims.\nrefl\nمَا نَنسَخۡ مِنۡ ءَايَةٍ أَوۡ نُنسِهَا نَأۡتِ بِخَيۡرٖ مِّنۡهَآ أَوۡ مِثۡلِهَآۗ أَلَمۡ تَعۡلَمۡ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٌ ١٠٦\nThe subject of abrogation is very important and indispensable to scholars; only ignorant fools deny it. Its importance lies in its effect on rulings on controversial issues and its role in recognizing the lawful and the unlawful. Al-Qurtubi: 2/300.\nKnowing the subject of abrogation is important for anyone who infers rules from the Quran and Islamic teachings. Why?\nأَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ لَهُ مُلْكُ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضِ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ مِنْ وَلِيٍّ وَلا نَصِيرٍ ١٠٧\nWhoever believes that Allah is his ally and defender and that there is no protector or supporter for him except Allah, will certainly know that everything Allah does is for his benefit; therefore, he entrusts all matters to Him. Al-Alusi: 1/354.\nWhat is the benefit to one who believes that Allah is his ally and supporter?\nأَمۡ تُرِيدُونَ أَن تَسۡٔلُواْ رَسُولَكُمۡ كَمَا سُئِلَ مُوسَىٰ مِن قَبۡلُۗ\nThis refers to questions raised due to stubbornness or objections, however, asking for the sake of guidance and understanding is praiseworthy and is enjoined by Allah. Al-Saadi: 62.\nWhen is raising questions about Islamic teachings considered good? When is it censured?\nوَدَّ كَثِيرٞ مِّنۡ أَهۡلِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَوۡ يَرُدُّونَكُم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ إِيمَٰنِكُمۡ كُفَّارًا حَسَدٗا مِّنۡ عِندِ أَنفُسِهِم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلۡحَقُّۖ\n(Many of the people of the Book wish), this verse came down explaining the situation of a Jewish leader (Huyay Ibn Akhtab) and his brother (Abu Yassir) and other Jews who were full of envy toward Muslims and tried, out of envy, to turn them away from their faith. Ibn Juzay: 1/78.\nWhat do you think about one who belittles the enmity of Jews and Christians toward Muslims, and accuses Muslims of believing in the theory of \"global conspiracy\"?\nبَلَىٰۚ مَنۡ أَسۡلَمَ وَجۡهَهُۥ لِلَّهِ وَهُوَ مُحۡسِنٞ فَلَهُۥٓ أَجۡرُهُۥ عِندَ رَبِّهِۦ وَلَا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ١١٢\n(On the contrary, whoever submits his face [himself] to Allah), means: He is sincere to Allah. (And he is a doer of good), means: He follows the Messenger (r). For there are two conditions for deeds to be accepted; the deed must be performed for Allah's sake alone and conform to Sharia. When a deed is performed sincerely, but does not conform to Sharia, then it will not be accepted. Ibn Kathir: 1/147.\nWhat are the conditions for accepting good deeds? What is the proof for that?\nبَلَىٰۚ مَنۡ أَسۡلَمَ وَجۡهَهُۥ لِلَّهِ وَهُوَ مُحۡسِنٞ فَلَهُۥٓ أَجۡرُهُۥ عِندَ رَبِّهِۦ وَلَا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ١١٢\n(Whoever submits himself to Allah), means that he is sincere to Allah alone in his deeds, and turns to Him with all his heart, (and) in addition to his sincerity, he (is a doer of good) with regard to worshiping his Lord, in that he worships Him as He has prescribed. Those who maintain these two attributes will be the sole people of Paradise. From this, we may understand that whoever is not like that will be among the doomed people of Hellfire, for there is no salvation except for those who are sincere to Allah and follow the Messenger (r). Al-Saadi: 64.\nA deed that is performed only to show off or that which is not done in accordance with Sharia is rejected. Why?\nبَلَىٰۚ مَنۡ أَسۡلَمَ وَجۡهَهُۥ لِلَّهِ وَهُوَ مُحۡسِنٞ فَلَهُۥٓ أَجۡرُهُۥ عِندَ رَبِّهِۦ وَلَا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ١١٢\nOnly he who submits his face to Allah will enter Paradise, which means: Sincerely devotes his religion to Allah, or he who sincerely worships Allah, or he who is subservient and humble to Allah. The essence of Islam is submission. The (face) is mentioned because when he submits his face in prostration, all of his limbs will follow. Al-Baghawi: 1/93.\nWho is entitled to enter Paradise by the grace of Allah?\nwords\nنَنسَخWe abrogate\nنُنسِهَاWe cause it to be forgotten\nسَوَاءَ السَّبِيلِMiddle of the road which is the Straight Path"],[18,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nCooperate with your brethren in tidying up a mosque to make it more appealing to others since this is considered honoring the symbols [rites] of Allah.\nStay in a mosque remembering Allah from the time of one prescribed prayer until the next one.\nRevive the Sunnah by performing a voluntary prayer while on board a car, a ship or an airplane, no matter where it is heading.\nguid\nAccusing others of being misguided requires valid proofs.\nBeware of preventing acts of worship in the houses of Allah, for it is a grave wrongdoing.\nThe Prophet (r) came with glad tidings and warnings. Focusing only on either glad tidings or warnings is wrong, but combining the effects of both is the right approach.\nrefl\nوَقَالَتِ ٱلۡيَهُودُ لَيۡسَتِ ٱلنَّصَٰرَىٰ عَلَىٰ شَيۡءٖ وَقَالَتِ ٱلنَّصَٰرَىٰ لَيۡسَتِ ٱلۡيَهُودُ عَلَىٰ شَيۡءٖ وَهُمۡ يَتۡلُونَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَۗ\nThey -as Imam Ahmad said- differ about the Book, oppose the Book, and agree to depart from the Book. They have combined the two descriptions of discord that Allah has condemned in His Book, for He has condemned those who oppose the Prophets and those who differ over the Prophets. Ibn Taimyah: 1/311.\nThe Jews and Christians combined two descriptions of discord. What are they?\nوَمَنۡ أَظۡلَمُ مِمَّن مَّنَعَ مَسَٰجِدَ ٱللَّهِ أَن يُذۡكَرَ فِيهَا ٱسۡمُهُۥ وَسَعَىٰ فِي خَرَابِهَآۚ\nAs there is no one who does greater evil than those who prevent the Name of Allah from being mentioned in His mosques, then there is no one who has greater faith than the one who strives to tend the mosques in both a physical and moral sense, as Allah says: (The mosques of Allah are only to be visited and tended by those who believe in Allah and the Last Day) [9-18]. Al-Saadi: 63.\nTending the mosques or destructing them are acts of a great significance to Allah. Explain.\nوَمَنۡ أَظۡلَمُ مِمَّن مَّنَعَ مَسَٰجِدَ ٱللَّهِ أَن يُذۡكَرَ فِيهَا ٱسۡمُهُۥ وَسَعَىٰ فِي خَرَابِهَآۚ\nOne of the signs of the coming of Day of Judgment is neglecting mosques, therefore, every nation, a group or a person who perpetrates an offense inside a mosque which causes it to be abandoned, Allah will punish him with terror and fear in this life. Al-Biqai: 1/225.\nNeglecting mosques is among the signs of the coming of Day of Judgment. How are they neglected?\nوَسَعَىٰ فِي خَرَابِهَآۚ\n(And strives), means: He tries hard and does his utmost (for their destruction) in both a physical and moral sense. Physical destruction means demolishing, ruining, and defiling them. Moral destruction means preventing people from mentioning Allah's name therein. The meaning of this verse is general and applies to anyone who meets this description. Al-Saadi: 63.\nDestructions of mosques? Which type is more common today?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ لَوۡلَا يُكَلِّمُنَا ٱللَّهُ أَوۡ تَأۡتِينَآ ءَايَةٞۗ\nThis is how they were with their Messengers: They would ask for signs out of obstinacy, and not for seeking guidance. Their aim was not to clarify the truth, as the Messengers had already brought signs that would make people believe. Al-Saadi: 64.\nThe disbelievers asked for signs, but Allah did not answer them. Why?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ لَوۡلَا يُكَلِّمُنَا ٱللَّهُ أَوۡ تَأۡتِينَآ ءَايَةٞۗ كَذَٰلِكَ قَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِم مِّثۡلَ قَوۡلِهِمۡۘ تَشَٰبَهَتۡ قُلُوبُهُمۡۗ\n(Their hearts resemble each other): The pronoun refers to those who do not know and to those before them, and their hearts are alike in disbelief, or in seeking what is not right to be sought. Ibn Juzay: 1/81.\nIn what way do the hearts of those (who do not know) resemble that of (those before them)?\nإِنَّآ أَرۡسَلۡنَٰكَ بِٱلۡحَقِّ بَشِيرٗا وَنَذِيرٗاۖ وَلَا تُسۡٔلُ عَنۡ أَصۡحَٰبِ ٱلۡجَحِيمِ ١١٩\nMeaning: We have sent you as a bearer of glad tidings to those who obey, and a warner to those who disobey, not to force anyone to accept faith, as there will be no blame on you if they persist in their disbelief. Al-Alusi: 1/370.\nFor one who invites others to Islam, what does he benefit from this verse?\nwords\nقَانِتُونَThey are submissive\nبَدِيعُOriginator"],[19,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nInferring from this verse and the events of current times, write a message or an article about the enmity of Jews and Christians toward Muslims, and their aim to make Muslims abandon their faith.\nWhen reciting or memorizing the Quran, set a goal to extract a deed from the verses and apply it in your life.\nSay, \"Our Lord grant us from among our wives and offspring comfort to our eyes and make us an example for the righteous.\"\nguid\nA Muslim will never be able to gain a full approval from non-Muslims unless he converts to their religion; therefore, he should only look to please Allah.\nThere is no true guidance except in the words of Allah and His Messenger (r); therefore, strive to reflect on them.\nProphet Abraham (u) was a leader of the guided and reformers because he fully carried out the responsibilities of Allah's commands. Whoever aspires to be a religious leader, should practice what he knows.\nrefl\nوَلَن تَرۡضَىٰ عَنكَ ٱلۡيَهُودُ وَلَا ٱلنَّصَٰرَىٰ حَتَّىٰ تَتَّبِعَ مِلَّتَهُمۡۗ\nTherefore, do not seek what pleases or satisfies them, rather, seek what pleases Allah by calling them to the truth with which Allah sent you. Ibn Kathir: 1/155.\nIf Jews and Christians will never be pleased with you, what is your duty toward them?\nوَلَن تَرۡضَىٰ عَنكَ ٱلۡيَهُودُ وَلَا ٱلنَّصَٰرَىٰ حَتَّىٰ تَتَّبِعَ مِلَّتَهُمۡۗ\nWhen the Jews and Christians asked for signs, it is not their aim, O Muhammad, to accept Islam even if you were to bring them everything they asked for, they would still not be pleased with you. They will only be pleased when you abandon Islam and follow them. Al-Qurtubi: 2/345.\nWhat is the purpose of the Jews and Christians behind their demands from Muslims?\nٱلَّذِينَ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُمُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ يَتۡلُونَهُۥ حَقَّ تِلَاوَتِهِۦٓ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِهِۦۗ\nReciting the Book (Holy Quran) means following its teachings, as Ibn Masoud said about this verse, (Those to whom We have given the Book recite it as it should be recited); he said: \"They enjoin what is lawful, forbid what is unlawful, believe in its unspecific verses and act upon its definite verses.\" Ibn Taimyah: 1/339.\nHow does one recite the Quran as it should be?\nوَإِذِ ٱبۡتَلَىٰٓ إِبۡرَٰهِۧمَ رَبُّهُۥ بِكَلِمَٰتٖ فَأَتَمَّهُنَّۖ قَالَ إِنِّي جَاعِلُكَ لِلنَّاسِ إِمَامٗاۖ قَالَ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِيۖ قَالَ لَا يَنَالُ عَهۡدِي ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٢٤\nA group of scholars inferred from this verse that the Imam (a Muslim Ruler) must be one of those who are known for justice, good conduct, virtue and has the ability to fulfill the task of leadership. Therefore, those who are known for iniquity, injustice and wrongdoing are not qualified because of this verse (My covenant does not include the wrongdoers). Al-Qurtubi: 2/370.\nWhat are the conditions for holding a leadership position in a Muslim country?\nوَإِذۡ جَعَلۡنَا ٱلۡبَيۡتَ مَثَابَةٗ لِّلنَّاسِ وَأَمۡنٗا\n(Mathabat'n): A place of return for the people. Whenever they are far away, they long to visit the Ka'bah again, which is a sign indicating that eventually they will all be leaving this life and return back to Allah. Al-Biqai: 1/239.\nWhat is meant by (A place of return for the people)?\nأَن طَهِّرَا بَيۡتِيَ لِلطَّآئِفِينَ وَٱلۡعَٰكِفِينَ وَٱلرُّكَّعِ ٱلسُّجُودِ ١٢٥\n(Those who bow and prostrate): These are when the servant is closest to Allah. Bowing and prostrating are the two greatest pillars of the prayer, and that is why when they are mentioned, they refer to the prayer as a whole. Al-Alusi: 1/381.\nBowing and prostrating are the two greatest pillars of the prayer. How do you know that?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ إِبۡرَٰهِۧمُ رَبِّ ٱجۡعَلۡ هَٰذَا بَلَدًا ءَامِنٗا وَٱرۡزُقۡ أَهۡلَهُۥ مِنَ ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ مَنۡ ءَامَنَ مِنۡهُم بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِۚ قَالَ وَمَن كَفَرَ فَأُمَتِّعُهُۥ قَلِيلٗا ثُمَّ أَضۡطَرُّهُۥٓ إِلَىٰ عَذَابِ ٱلنَّارِۖ وَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡمَصِيرُ ١٢٦\nAllah is teaching His Prophet Abraham (u) that provision is not provided exclusively to the believers, but rather, it is a general mercy from Allah to all who live in this world, unlike religious leadership (Imamah) which is exclusive to the sincerest believers. Al-Alusi: 1/382.\nIs the provision of Allah in this world provided exclusively to the believers?\nwords\nمَثَابَةًA place of return for the people\nأَضطَرُّهُI compel him\nالمَصِيرُFinal return to Allah"],[20,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nRecall some good deeds you have done in the past, and with each deed say: [\"Our Lord, accept [this] from us. Indeed, You are the Hearing, the Knowing\"].\nSupplicate Allah, today, and include your descendants in it.\nWhile keeping your Quran recitation time, try, today, to start reading Sunnah references such as Sahih Al-Bukhari and Sahih Muslim.\nguid\nPraying for descendants to become followers of the straight path is practiced by Prophets and righteous people.\nWhenever you do an act of worship, say: [\"Our Lord, accept [this] from us. Indeed, You are the Hearing, the Knowing\"].\nThe Prophets used to ask Allah to accept their repentance, and we are in a greater need to do that.\nrefl\nوَإِذۡ يَرۡفَعُ إِبۡرَٰهِۧمُ ٱلۡقَوَاعِدَ مِنَ ٱلۡبَيۡتِ وَإِسۡمَٰعِيلُ رَبَّنَا تَقَبَّلۡ مِنَّآۖ\n(Accept from us): Treat us with Your grace, and do not turn down our efforts; this is a sign of acknowledgment of their shortcomings, and the insignificance of the servant -even if he strives- in comparison to the greatness of Allah. Al-Biqai: 1/242.\nWhy did Abraham and Ishmael ask Allah to accept their efforts?\nوَإِذۡ يَرۡفَعُ إِبۡرَٰهِۧمُ ٱلۡقَوَاعِدَ مِنَ ٱلۡبَيۡتِ وَإِسۡمَٰعِيلُ رَبَّنَا تَقَبَّلۡ مِنَّآۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ١٢٧\nThe present tense form is used, (is raising), even though this story was in the past, is to highlight the importance of this matter so that people would follow Prophet Abraham's example in carrying out difficult acts of obedience while asking Allah to accept them, and for them to recognize the greatness of the house of Allah (Ka'bah) and honor it. Al-Alusi: 1/383.\nWhy is present tense form (is raising) used even though this story was in the past?\nرَبَّنَا وَٱجۡعَلۡنَا مُسۡلِمَيۡنِ لَكَ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِنَآ أُمَّةٗ مُّسۡلِمَةٗ لَّكَ وَأَرِنَا مَنَاسِكَنَا وَتُبۡ عَلَيۡنَآۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلتَّوَّابُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ١٢٨\nAs it is the case that human beings, no matter how hard they try, will always fall short and need to repent. They (Abraham and Ishmael) said, (and accept our repentance. Indeed, You are the Accepting of Repentance, the Merciful). Al-Saadi: 66.\nWhy did they ask for acceptance of repentance even though they have a high status as Prophets?\nرَبَّنَا وَٱجۡعَلۡنَا مُسۡلِمَيۡنِ لَكَ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِنَآ أُمَّةٗ مُّسۡلِمَةٗ لَّكَ وَأَرِنَا مَنَاسِكَنَا وَتُبۡ عَلَيۡنَآۖ\nRepentance varies according to those who repent; repentance of general Muslims is showing remorse, intending not to re-commit the sin again and giving back to others (and if not possible, then intending to give back) what was taken from them. The Repentance of the elite Muslims is turning away from disliked actions such as bad thoughts, slackness in good deeds, and imperfect acts of worship. The Repentance of the favored Muslims is for elevation of status and higher ranks with Allah. Al-Alusi: 1/386.\nDoes repentance differ from one person to another? Explain.\nرَبَّنَا وَٱبۡعَثۡ فِيهِمۡ رَسُولٗا مِّنۡهُمۡ يَتۡلُواْ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتِكَ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ\n(Wisdom) is the knowledge of religion, knowledge of interpretation, and understanding, which is a trait and a light from Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 2/403.\nAbraham (u) supplicated Allah for (Wisdom). What does it mean?\nرَبَّنَا وَٱبۡعَثۡ فِيهِمۡ رَسُولٗا مِّنۡهُمۡ يَتۡلُواْ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتِكَ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ وَيُزَكِّيهِمۡۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ١٢٩\n(Wisdom) is Prophet Muhammad's (r) Sunnah because Allah commanded the wives of Prophet Muhammad (r) to remember what is recited in their houses of the verses of Allah and wisdom. Verses of Allah are the Holy Quran. Everything else of what the Prophet conveyed is his Sunnah. Ibn Taimyah: 1/345.\nWhat is meant by (Wisdom)? How can we infer that?\nفَلَا تَمُوتُنَّ إِلَّا وَأَنتُم مُّسۡلِمُونَ ١٣٢\nAdhere to it, follow it and mold your character in accordance with its teachings, so that you may persist in that. Do not let death come to you except when you are steadfast in that, since whoever lives his life following something, will die in that state; and whoever dies following something, will be resurrected in the same state. Al-Saadi: 67.\nAllah commands them to die as Muslims even though a person cannot control himself when he dies. How?\nwords\nالقَوَاعِدَFoundations\nوَأَرِنَا مَنَاسِكَنَاShow us our rites (of worship)\nوَيُزَكِّيهِمHe purifies them\nيَرغَبُOne who would be averse\nسَفِهَ نَفسَهُOne who makes a fool of himself"],[21,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nAlways ask Allah for guidance.\nRecite this verse in the first rak'a of the Sunnah before Al-Fajr prayer.\nDeclare the truth to the people and show your commitment to it, as this is more likely to lead to steadfastness and people's acceptance of it.\nguid\nThe believer should not be concerned by slogans and claims nor be tempted by words. Rather, he should search for facts backed by proofs.\nThere is no guidance or happiness in this world and the next except through Islam.\nA Muslim must demonstrate his correct belief, proclaim it, and call people to it, as it is the essence and foundation of the religion.\nrefl\nقُولُوٓاْ ءَامَنَّا بِٱللَّهِ\n(Say) means: Speak verbally what is in your hearts. This is what entails reward, because just as uttering words without belief in the heart is hypocrisy and disbelief, similarly, mere words that have no basis in belief will have no impact and are of little benefit. Al-Saadi: 67.\nIs faith (Iman) realized by mere words?\nقُولُوٓاْ ءَامَنَّا بِٱللَّهِ وَمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡنَا وَمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَىٰٓ إِبۡرَٰهِۧمَ وَإِسۡمَٰعِيلَ وَإِسۡحَٰقَ وَيَعۡقُوبَ وَٱلۡأَسۡبَاطِ وَمَآ أُوتِيَ مُوسَىٰ وَعِيسَىٰ وَمَآ أُوتِيَ ٱلنَّبِيُّونَ مِن رَّبِّهِمۡ\nThe belief in Allah is mentioned first because it is the same in all true Sharias (divine laws); then, the belief in all revealed Sharias from Allah is mentioned. Ibn Ashur: 1/739.\nWhy is the belief in Allah mentioned before the belief in revealed Sharias?\nوَمَآ أُوتِيَ ٱلنَّبِيُّونَ مِن رَّبِّهِمۡ\nThis indicates that the gift of religious commitment is the true gift that is connected to happiness in this world and the Hereafter. Allah does not instruct us to believe in what was given to the Prophets such as kingship, wealth and the like; rather, He commands us to believe in what they were given of books and laws. Al-Saadi: 68.\nWho, from among the people, has received the most favors from Allah?\nفَإِنۡ ءَامَنُواْ بِمِثۡلِ مَآ ءَامَنتُم بِهِۦ فَقَدِ ٱهۡتَدَواْۖ وَّإِن تَوَلَّوۡاْ فَإِنَّمَا هُمۡ فِي شِقَاقٖۖ فَسَيَكۡفِيكَهُمُ ٱللَّهُۚ وَهُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ١٣٧\n(Allah will suffice you against them): This was a fulfilled promise. The Jews of Bani Quraithah were neutralized, the Jews of Bani An-Nadir were expelled, etc. Ibn Juzay: 1/85.\nGive three examples where Allah sufficed His Prophet (r) against the disbelievers.\nصِبۡغَةَ ٱللَّهِ وَمَنۡ أَحۡسَنُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ صِبۡغَةٗۖ وَنَحۡنُ لَهُۥ عَٰبِدُونَ ١٣٨\nMeaning: Adhere to the color given by Allah, which is His religion, and follow it completely, both inward and outward, with all of its beliefs at all times, so that it will become like a color for you, and one of your characteristics. Once it becomes one of your characteristics, then you will follow its instructions willingly and lovingly, and religious commitment will become second nature to you, like the color of a garment which has become an integral part of it. Thus, you will attain happiness in this world and the Hereafter. Al-Saadi: 68.\nWhy is religion called (color of Allah) in this verse?\nوَنَحۡنُ لَهُۥ عَٰبِدُونَ ١٣٨\nSaeed bin Jubair said: Sincerity is to devote one's faith and deeds to Allah alone, where he does not associate partners with Allah and does not make show of his deeds. Fudhail bin Iyadh said: Abandoning a good deed for people's sake is a showoff, performing a good deed for people's sake is (minor) Shirk, and true sincerity is to be saved by Allah from both. Al-Baghawi: 1/113.\nWhat is true sincerity to Allah?\nتِلۡكَ أُمَّةٞ قَدۡ خَلَتۡۖ لَهَا مَا كَسَبَتۡ وَلَكُم مَّا كَسَبۡتُمۡۖ وَلَا تُسۡٔلُونَ عَمَّا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ١٤١\nThis verse is repeated because it contains a threat, which means that if the Prophets, despite their virtue and leadership, will be recompensed for their actions, then, it will be even more so for you all. Al-Qurtubi: 2/425.\nThis verse is repeated twice. Why?\nwords\nوَالأَسبَاطِProphets descending from Prophet Jacob, (Israelites)\nشِقَاقٍPlain Dissention\nصِبغَةَ اللَّهِReligion of Allah"]])